# Captured evidence never goes into git history.
#
# evidence/ holds .wer crash reports, systeminfo (hostname, BIOS, install date),
# full driver inventories, and shell event logs. watch/ output holds process
# dumps and ETW traces. All of it is machine-identifying and some of it is
# gigabytes. Once committed it is permanent, so it is excluded from the very
# first commit rather than scrubbed later.

evidence/
captures/
slow-capture/
dwm-capture/
*.dmp
*.etl
*.wer
*.csv

# Local instrument state
dwm-growth.csv
dwm-growth-trigger.log
ui-response.csv
task-*.vbs
*.flag

# TraceProcessor SDK binaries (Microsoft.Windows.EventTracing*.dll) that
# dwm-pmc-verify.ps1 / dwm-pmc-occlusion.ps1 load from -TraceProcessorLibDir.
# Third-party NuGet output, not source -- fetch it per README rather than
# committing it.
watch/lib/

